  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The L3 oral exposure records concern 6-β-naltrexol (M01) and ethinylestradiol (M02), not nalbuphine; they report Cmax/AUC values without an IV comparator or absolute bioavailability estimate, so they do not provide threshold-relevant F evidence for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C24", "C25", "C26", "C27", "C28", "C29", "C30", "C31", "C32", "C33", "C34", "C35"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Meptazinol, the closest non-cirrhotic phenolic-opioid comparator, has a cirrhotic F of 27.9±5.3% that is a four-fold increase over controls, giving an inferred control F of about 7%; this supports F<20% for a similarly first-pass-liable phenolic opioid such as nalbuphine.",
      "card_ids": ["C19", "C23"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The high-F opioid contexts are cirrhosis-dependent (pentazocine, meperidine) or structurally distinct (ciramadol, paliperidone, haloperidol, BI 425809, ACT-1004-1239, UDCA), so they do not affirm F≥20% for the non-cirrhotic query.",
      "card_ids": ["C10", "C16", "C17", "C18", "C20", "C01", "C03", "C08", "C09", "C12"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C24", "C25", "C26", "C27", "C28", "C29", "C30", "C31", "C32", "C33", "C34", "C35"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct nalbuphine-specific absolute oral bioavailability measurement is present in the supplied records.",
    "The meptazinol control F (~7%) is inferred from the stated four-fold increase over controls rather than reported as a direct numeric control value.",
    "L3 exposure records are for naltrexol and ethinylestradiol, not nalbuphine, and lack IV-comparator F estimates.",
    "Normal-condition F values for pentazocine, meperidine, and ciramadol are not directly provided; ciramadol's high F in cirrhosis with P>0.05 complicates a simple phenolic-opioid class analogy.",
    "The extent of nalbuphine's first-pass glucuronidation is not quantified in the supplied evidence."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L3 oral exposure records (naltrexol and ethinylestradiol Cmax/AUC) are not nalbuphine F measurements and do not alter the L2 evidence balance. The most transferable non-cirrhotic comparator, meptazinol, has an inferred F of about 7%, supporting F<20% for this first-pass-liable phenolic morphinan; high-F contexts are cirrhosis-dependent or structurally unrelated. Prediction remains low with moderate confidence."
}

